                        "review": "I honestly wanted to like this game, but I cannot recommend it. Partially due to me problem and mostly due to the state of the game.\n\nThe Me issue: As far as I had understood, this game would fall into a vein similiar to other \"mercenary games\", like Battle Brothers, Fell Seal or Wartales or the plethora of \"Tactics\" games out there, with a class system allowing for costumization and personalization, and as the devs promised, the characters would age and change over time as the years go on in game. Well I must have misunderstood something because the game is really restrictive as far as costumization and classes go, each class is locked to a gender and type of equipment and set of abilities, as well as how they look. If I want a male Valkyrie? Out of luck. Fire Mage using say, an axe or sword? No. The aging aspect also isn't in the game...or just really underwhelming. Or I just didn't play far enough. So I will concede that it's partly me probably misunderstanding the marketing material.\n\nThe state of the game: However, the game isn't finished. The Story just stops, the factions aren't implemented, the last class they promised never got implemented, more character costumization that was promised wasn't implemented. The game has some weird performance issues despite being 2D Pixel graphics, running more sluggish at times than games with full 3D engines. And none of this will probably change since the devs stated that they ran out of money to work full time on this game, and the former publisher Humble Games imploded and went under.\n\nDamn shame.",
